<title>USA: FEDEX SEEKS TO MEET DEMAND FROM UPS STRIKE.</title>
<headline>FEDEX SEEKS TO MEET DEMAND FROM UPS STRIKE.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Express Corp said Wednesday that its delivery service is &quot;stretched to its limits,&quot; and it has implemented additional temporary measures to try to keep up with increased demand in the wake of the ongoing strike at United Parcel Service of America.</p>
<p>The company said that until now, it has managed and controlled the increased volume.</p>
<p>However, as the strike continues, UPS customers are trying to switch more business to Federal Express, causing possible volume-related delays, it said.</p>
</text>
